[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"Local Storage Solutions in Flutter: Hive, Isar, Drift, and Secure Storage"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"Choosing the right local storage solution is critical for building performant and reliable Flutter applications. Depending on your use case—whether it is storing simple key-value pairs, complex relational data, or highly sensitive user credentials—Flutter offers a variety of robust packages. This tutorial explores four of the most popular local storage options: Hive, Isar, Drift, and Flutter Secure Storage."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"1. Hive: Lightweight NoSQL Key-Value Database"},{"order":4,"type":"paragraph","text":"Hive is a lightweight and blazing-fast NoSQL database written purely in Dart. It is designed for simple data models and key-value storage. Because it does not rely on native binaries (like SQLite), it works seamlessly across mobile, desktop, and web platforms."},{"order":5,"type":"code","text":"import 'package:hive_flutter/hive_flutter.dart';

void main() async {
  await Hive.initFlutter();
  var box = await Hive.openBox('settingsBox');
  box.put('darkMode', true);
  bool isDarkMode = box.get('darkMode', defaultValue: false);
}"},{"order":6,"type":"subheading","text":"2. Isar: The Successor to Hive with Advanced Querying"},{"order":7,"type":"paragraph","text":"Isar is developed by the same author as Hive, but it is built as a super-fast, ACID-compliant NoSQL document database built specifically for Flutter. Unlike Hive, Isar supports complex queries, secondary indexes, multi-entry indexes, and full-text search out of the box."},{"order":8,"type":"code","text":"import 'package:isar/isar.dart';

part 'user.g.dart';

@Collection()
class User {
  Id id = Isar.autoIncrement;

  @Index(caseSensitive: false)
  late String name;

  late int age;
}"},{"order":9,"type":"subheading","text":"3. Drift: Robust Type-Safe SQLite for Relational Data"},{"order":10,"type":"paragraph","text":"Drift (formerly Moor) is a reactive persistence library built on top of SQLite. It allows you to write type-safe Dart queries or write raw SQL. Drift is ideal for applications that require complex relational schemas, foreign keys, and transactions."},{"order":11,"type":"code","text":"import 'package:drift/drift.dart';

class Todos extends Table {
  IntColumn get id => integer().autoIncrement()();
  TextColumn get title => text().withLength(min: 6, max: 32)();
  BoolColumn get completed => boolean().withDefault(const Constant(false))();
}"},{"order":12,"type":"subheading","text":"4. Flutter Secure Storage: Encrypted Storage for Sensitive Data"},{"order":13,"type":"paragraph","text":"None of the above databases are inherently secure for storing sensitive data like OAuth tokens, passwords, or cryptographic keys. Flutter Secure Storage provides API to store data securely using Keychain (on iOS) and EncryptedSharedPreferences (on Android)."},{"order":14,"type":"code","text":"import 'package:flutter_secure_storage/flutter_secure_storage.dart';

final storage = const FlutterSecureStorage();

// Write value
await storage.write(key: 'auth_token', value: 'secret_token_123');

// Read value
String? token = await storage.read(key: 'auth_token');"},{"order":15,"type":"subheading","text":"Summary and Best Practices"},{"order":16,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Use Hive or Isar for general application state, offline caching, and documents."},{"order":17,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Use Drift when your data model is heavily relational with complex queries and joins."},{"order":18,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Always use Flutter Secure Storage for tokens, API keys, and sensitive user credentials."}]
